WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
FilmSub.lk — සිංහල උපසිරැසි සමඟ (Auto Sinhala Subtitles)

00:01:55.575 --> 00:01:57.660
(BOTH YELLING)

00:02:10.173 --> 00:02:12.217
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:02:13.051 --> 00:02:15.136
Well struck.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:16.888
Well struck, dog.

00:02:21.226 --> 00:02:22.727
Did you like that?

00:02:22.811 --> 00:02:24.687
It was well struck, Your Grace.

00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:27.232
I already said it was well struck.

00:02:28.233 --> 00:02:30.193
Yes, Your Grace.

00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:40.203
- Who's next? - HERALD: Lothor Brune,

00:02:40.286 --> 00:02:43.498
freerider in the service of Lord Baelish.

00:02:43.581 --> 00:02:46.751
Ser Dontos the Red of House Hollard.

00:02:49.671 --> 00:02:52.465
Ser Dontos the Red of House Hollard!

00:02:52.549 --> 00:02:53.967
DONTOS: Here I am.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.052
Here I am.

00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:03.893
Sorry, Your Grace.

00:03:04.811 --> 00:03:06.688
My deepest apologies.

00:03:06.771 --> 00:03:08.398
- JOFFREY: Are you drunk? - No.

00:03:09.065 --> 00:03:11.192
No. No, Your Grace.

00:03:11.276 --> 00:03:13.862
- I had two cups of wine. - Two cups?

00:03:13.945 --> 00:03:15.864
That's not much at all.

00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:18.575
Please, have another cup.

00:03:18.658 --> 00:03:20.118
Are you sure, Your Grace?

00:03:20.201 --> 00:03:22.495
Yes. To celebrate my name day.

00:03:22.579 --> 00:03:24.998
Have two. Have as much as you like.

00:03:26.332 --> 00:03:27.917
I would be honored, Your Grace.

00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:32.630
Ser Meryn, help Ser Dontos celebrate my name day.

00:03:33.339 --> 00:03:34.757
See that he drinks his fill.

00:03:37.302 --> 00:03:38.344
(CROWD GASPS)

00:03:50.148 --> 00:03:52.317
(GURGLING)

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.903
You can't.

00:03:55.486 --> 00:03:57.113
What did you say?

00:03:58.448 --> 00:04:00.241
Did you say I can't?

00:04:00.325 --> 00:04:01.910
I only meant

00:04:01.993 --> 00:04:04.871
it would be bad luck to kill a man on your name day.

00:04:04.954 --> 00:04:07.123
What kind of stupid peasant's superstition...

00:04:07.665 --> 00:04:09.042
HOUND: The girl is right.

00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:12.420
What a man sows on his name day, he reaps all year.

00:04:12.503 --> 00:04:14.213
- (MEN LAUGHING) - (WINE POURING)

00:04:14.297 --> 00:04:15.798
(JOFFREY SIGHS)

00:04:15.882 --> 00:04:17.383
Take him away.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.510
I'll have him killed tomorrow, the fool.

00:04:21.012 --> 00:04:22.221
(CROWD MURMURING)

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:26.142
He is a fool. You're so clever to see it.

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:29.395
He'll make a much better fool than a knight.

00:04:29.479 --> 00:04:32.482
He doesn't deserve the mercy of a quick death.

00:04:34.192 --> 00:04:36.986
Did you hear my lady, Ser Dontos?

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:40.114
From this day, you'll be my new fool.

00:04:40.198 --> 00:04:42.408
Thank you, Your Grace.

00:04:42.492 --> 00:04:45.620
And you, my lady, thank you.

00:04:45.703 --> 00:04:47.372
TYRION: Beloved nephew.

00:04:54.796 --> 00:04:57.423
We looked for you on the battlefield.

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:02.053
You were nowhere to be found.

00:05:03.554 --> 00:05:05.640
I've been here, ruling the kingdoms.

00:05:05.723 --> 00:05:08.393
What a fine job you've done.

00:05:09.394 --> 00:05:10.561
Look at you.

00:05:12.105 --> 00:05:14.190
More beautiful than ever.

00:05:14.273 --> 00:05:15.984
And you!

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:18.319
You're going to be bigger than the Hound,

00:05:18.403 --> 00:05:20.822
- but much better looking. - (LAUGHS)

00:05:20.905 --> 00:05:22.824
This one doesn't like me.

00:05:22.907 --> 00:05:24.742
Can't imagine why.

00:05:24.826 --> 00:05:27.328
- We heard you were dead. - I'm glad you're not dead.

00:05:28.371 --> 00:05:30.999
Me, too, dear. Death is so boring,

00:05:31.082 --> 00:05:34.377
especially now, with so much excitement in the world.

00:05:35.378 --> 00:05:36.713
My lady, I'm sorry for your loss.

00:05:38.589 --> 00:05:39.841
Her loss?

00:05:39.924 --> 00:05:41.843
Her father was a confessed traitor.

00:05:41.926 --> 00:05:43.511
But still her father.

00:05:43.594 --> 00:05:46.264
Surely, having so recently lost your own beloved father, you can sympathize.

00:05:51.602 --> 00:05:53.438
My father was a traitor.

00:05:53.521 --> 00:05:55.398
My mother and brother are traitors, too.

00:05:55.898 --> 00:05:57.984
I am loyal to my beloved Joffrey.

00:05:59.819 --> 00:06:01.946
Of course you are.

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.827
Well, enjoy your name day, Your Grace.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.579
Wish I could stay and celebrate,

00:06:09.662 --> 00:06:12.457
but there is work to be done.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:14.542
What work?

00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:16.586
Why are you here?

00:06:20.298 --> 00:06:24.677
PYCELLE: A raven arrived from the citadel this morning, Your Grace.

00:06:24.761 --> 00:06:25.928
(BIRD SQUAWKING)

00:06:26.012 --> 00:06:27.597
The conclave has met,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.142
considered reports from maesters all over the Seven Kingdoms,

00:06:31.851 --> 00:06:34.353
and declared this great summer

00:06:34.771 --> 00:06:37.273
done at last.

00:06:37.356 --> 00:06:40.151
The longest summer in living memory.

00:06:40.526 --> 00:06:43.780
The peasants say, a long summer means an even longer winter.

00:06:43.863 --> 00:06:45.615
PYCELLE: A common superstition.

00:06:45.698 --> 00:06:48.076
LITTLEFINGER: We have enough wheat for a five-year winter.

00:06:48.159 --> 00:06:50.495
If it lasts any longer,

00:06:51.079 --> 00:06:53.039
we'll have fewer peasants.

00:06:53.122 --> 00:06:56.501
The city's drowning in refugees, Your Grace, fleeing the war.

00:06:56.584 --> 00:06:59.629
We have nowhere to house them. And with winter coming, it'll only get worse.

00:06:59.712 --> 00:07:03.007
You command the city watch, do you not, Lord Slynt?

00:07:04.342 --> 00:07:06.094
I do, Your Grace.

00:07:06.177 --> 00:07:08.179
And are you not a lord at my command?

00:07:08.262 --> 00:07:11.849
I owe my title and lands to your generosity, Your Grace.

00:07:11.933 --> 00:07:14.435
Then do your job. Shut the gates to the peasants.

00:07:14.519 --> 00:07:17.438
They belong in the field, not our capital.

00:07:17.522 --> 00:07:19.107
Yes, Your Grace.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.525
(TYRION WHISTLING TUNE)

00:07:25.863 --> 00:07:26.906
Don't get up.

00:07:28.366 --> 00:07:31.953
More ravishing than ever, big sister.

00:07:33.454 --> 00:07:35.915
War agrees with you.

00:07:35.998 --> 00:07:38.543
Forgive the interruption. Carry on.

00:07:40.378 --> 00:07:41.504
What are you doing here?

00:07:42.463 --> 00:07:45.216
It's been a remarkable journey.

00:07:45.842 --> 00:07:48.886
I pissed off the edge of the Wall,

00:07:49.887 --> 00:07:51.806
I slept in a sky cell,

00:07:51.889 --> 00:07:54.058
I fought with the hill tribes.

00:07:54.142 --> 00:07:55.685
So many adventures,

00:07:56.894 --> 00:07:59.522
so much to be thankful for.

00:07:59.605 --> 00:08:03.484
What are you doing here? This is the small council.

00:08:03.568 --> 00:08:08.322
Yes, well, I do believe the Hand of the King is welcome at all small council meetings.

00:08:08.406 --> 00:08:10.116
Our father is Hand of the King.

00:08:10.199 --> 00:08:13.202
Yes, but in his absence...

00:08:20.585 --> 00:08:22.879
VARYS: Your father has named Lord Tyrion

00:08:22.962 --> 00:08:25.506
to serve as hand in his stead while he fights.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.009
Out! All of you out!

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:35.558
I would like to know how you tricked Father into this.

00:08:35.641 --> 00:08:39.187
If I were capable of tricking Father, I'd be emperor of the world by now.

00:08:39.896 --> 00:08:41.814
You brought this on yourself.

00:08:42.273 --> 00:08:43.316
I've done nothing.

00:08:43.399 --> 00:08:45.193
Quite right, you did nothing

00:08:45.276 --> 00:08:47.528
when your son called for Ned Stark's head.

00:08:47.612 --> 00:08:49.530
Now the entire North has risen up against us.

00:08:49.614 --> 00:08:52.033
- I tried to stop it. - Did you? You failed.

00:08:52.116 --> 00:08:55.328
That bit of theater will haunt our family for a generation.

00:08:55.411 --> 00:08:59.290
- Robb Stark is a child. - Who's won every battle he's fought.

00:08:59.957 --> 00:09:01.709
Do you understand we're losing the war?

00:09:01.792 --> 00:09:04.879
- What do you know about warfare? - Nothing.

00:09:04.962 --> 00:09:06.714
But I know people.

00:09:06.797 --> 00:09:11.469
And I know that our enemies hate each other almost as much as they hate us.

00:09:16.098 --> 00:09:18.726
- Joffrey is king. - Joffrey is king.

00:09:19.477 --> 00:09:21.145
You are here to advise him.

00:09:21.229 --> 00:09:22.897
I'm only here to advise him.

00:09:23.397 --> 00:09:25.483
And if the king listens to what I say,

00:09:25.566 --> 00:09:29.070
the king might just get his Uncle Jaime back.

00:09:30.905 --> 00:09:32.323
How?

00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:33.950
You love your children.

00:09:34.033 --> 00:09:37.078
It's your one redeeming quality. That and your cheekbones.

00:09:38.496 --> 00:09:41.415
The Starks love their children as well.

00:09:41.499 --> 00:09:43.709
- And we have two of them. - One.

00:09:45.628 --> 00:09:48.422
- One? - Arya, little animal, she disappeared.

00:09:48.506 --> 00:09:51.509
Disappeared? What, in a puff of smoke?

00:09:53.636 --> 00:09:56.555
We had three Starks to trade.

00:09:56.639 --> 00:09:59.267
You chopped one's head off and let another escape.

00:10:00.351 --> 00:10:02.353
Father will be furious.

00:10:03.521 --> 00:10:04.981
It must be odd for you

00:10:07.525 --> 00:10:09.944
to be the disappointing child.

00:10:17.618 --> 00:10:21.247
LEADRANACH: My lord, may the old gods watch over your brother

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.958
and all our Northern sons.

00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:27.878
The walls of my holdfast will not stand the winter.

00:10:27.962 --> 00:10:32.091
The stones were last mortared in the time of King Aerys,

00:10:32.174 --> 00:10:36.762
and I'm afraid the masons today are not fit to carry their fathers' hammers.

00:10:38.055 --> 00:10:39.598
When I was a boy,

00:10:39.682 --> 00:10:45.062
I remember seeing them put up a new tower at Torrhen's Square in a summer.

00:10:45.146 --> 00:10:47.106
Men worked back then.

00:10:47.189 --> 00:10:52.486
Today, my holdfast looks like it was built by drunk children.

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:56.657
At night you can hear the wind howling through the gaps.

00:10:57.366 --> 00:10:58.993
Gods forbid it rains.

00:10:59.076 --> 00:11:01.912
Why, I might as well sleep beneath a waterfall.

00:11:01.996 --> 00:11:06.917
Maintenance of a holdfast generally falls to the lord of that holdfast.

00:11:07.084 --> 00:11:08.502
Generally, yes,

00:11:08.586 --> 00:11:12.006
but I've sent all the young men off to fight Robb Stark's war.

00:11:12.089 --> 00:11:15.217
King Robb. And it's not his war.

00:11:15.301 --> 00:11:17.178
He didn't choose it.

00:11:17.261 --> 00:11:20.765
Maybe not, my lord, but he called in his banners and took the men.

00:11:20.848 --> 00:11:22.516
Joffrey killed my father,

00:11:23.142 --> 00:11:25.019
your liege lord.

00:11:25.102 --> 00:11:27.480
Do you remember your vows, ser?

00:11:27.563 --> 00:11:29.398
Of course I remember!

00:11:29.482 --> 00:11:32.526
We can spare four masons for a week, my lord.

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:35.571
Will that be sufficient to repair your walls?

00:11:35.654 --> 00:11:37.698
I believe it will.

00:11:43.913 --> 00:11:46.624
We didn't want him here all day, did we?

00:11:47.541 --> 00:11:50.503
I didn't like the way he was talking about Robb.

00:11:50.586 --> 00:11:52.254
Nor did I.

00:11:54.715 --> 00:11:57.593
But listening to people you'd rather not listen to

00:11:57.676 --> 00:12:01.555
is one of your responsibilities as Lord of Winterfell.

00:12:01.639 --> 00:12:03.307
(BRAN SIGHS)

00:12:05.142 --> 00:12:06.894
Lord Portan.

00:12:06.977 --> 00:12:09.897
My lord, may the old gods watch over your brother

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.649
and all our Northern sons.

00:12:13.818 --> 00:12:15.903
(HEAVY BREATHING)

00:12:22.284 --> 00:12:24.036
- (WINGS FLAPPING) - (BIRD SQUAWKING)

00:13:00.656 --> 00:13:04.034
Boil this for an hour and drink the tea.

00:13:05.161 --> 00:13:07.538
Makes all your pain go away.

00:13:07.621 --> 00:13:09.123
BRAN: Don't have any pain.

00:13:10.249 --> 00:13:11.709
Lucky for you.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.295
That way.

00:13:17.548 --> 00:13:19.800
You've been having those dreams again.

00:13:19.884 --> 00:13:21.552
BRAN: I don't dream.

00:13:21.635 --> 00:13:23.137
Everyone dreams.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.805
I don't.

00:13:26.223 --> 00:13:28.225
Heard some of the men talking about the comet.

00:13:29.018 --> 00:13:30.519
They say it's an omen.

00:13:30.603 --> 00:13:34.023
They say it means Robb will win a great victory in the South.

00:13:34.106 --> 00:13:35.566
Did they?

00:13:37.651 --> 00:13:41.155
I heard some other fools say it's Lannister Red.

00:13:41.238 --> 00:13:44.408
Means the Lannisters will rule all Seven Kingdoms before long.

00:13:44.492 --> 00:13:47.953
Heard a stable boy say it's the color of blood

00:13:48.037 --> 00:13:50.206
to mark the death of your father.

00:13:54.168 --> 00:13:57.338
The stars don't fall for men.

00:13:57.421 --> 00:13:59.882
Red comet means one thing, boy.

00:14:01.175 --> 00:14:02.593
Dragons.

00:14:04.637 --> 00:14:07.348
The dragons are all dead.

00:14:07.431 --> 00:14:09.767
They've been dead for centuries.

00:14:42.675 --> 00:14:44.260
(SHRIEKS)

00:14:46.804 --> 00:14:48.055
Mmm.

00:14:53.143 --> 00:14:55.729
What did your brother say about them, Khaleesi?

00:14:55.813 --> 00:14:57.481
He said they ate meat.

00:14:57.565 --> 00:15:00.150
He didn't tell you what kind of meat?

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.238
My brother didn't know anything about dragons.

00:15:04.321 --> 00:15:07.324
He didn't know anything about anything.

00:15:12.413 --> 00:15:13.414
Eh.

00:15:16.667 --> 00:15:17.668
(WHINNIES)

00:15:20.963 --> 00:15:22.423
(WOMEN MURMURING)

00:15:41.275 --> 00:15:43.235
She was Drogo's first gift to me.

00:15:44.361 --> 00:15:46.030
I remember.

00:15:48.198 --> 00:15:50.784
I promised to protect them.

00:15:50.868 --> 00:15:53.120
Promised them their enemies would die screaming.

00:15:53.203 --> 00:15:55.581
How do I make starvation scream?

00:15:55.873 --> 00:15:58.375
A trick I never learned, I'm afraid.

00:16:00.544 --> 00:16:02.713
Does it ever end?

00:16:02.796 --> 00:16:04.632
This is further east than I've ever been.

00:16:04.715 --> 00:16:07.801
But, yes, Khaleesi, everything ends, even the Red Waste.

00:16:07.885 --> 00:16:10.304
And you're sure there's no other way?

00:16:10.387 --> 00:16:13.015
If we go south to the land of the Lhazareen,

00:16:13.098 --> 00:16:15.601
the Lamb Men will kill us and take your dragons.

00:16:15.684 --> 00:16:17.478
If we go west to the Dothraki Sea,

00:16:17.561 --> 00:16:21.148
the first khalasar we meet will kill us and take your dragons.

00:16:21.231 --> 00:16:23.651
No one will take my dragons.

00:16:25.027 --> 00:16:27.655
They are too weak to fight,

00:16:27.738 --> 00:16:29.823
as are your people.

00:16:29.907 --> 00:16:31.992
You must be their strength.

00:16:33.077 --> 00:16:35.037
As you are mine.

00:16:39.041 --> 00:16:40.459
(SPEAKS DOTHRAKI)

00:16:47.257 --> 00:16:51.679
Rakharo, Aggo, Kovarro. Take our remaining horses.

00:16:51.804 --> 00:16:56.183
You will ride east, you southeast, and you northeast.

00:16:56.892 --> 00:16:59.561
What do we seek, Khaleesi?

00:16:59.728 --> 00:17:05.776
Cities, living or dead. Caravans and people. Rivers or lakes or the great salt sea.

00:17:06.777 --> 00:17:11.448
Find how far the Red Waste extends before us, and what lies on the other side.

00:17:11.824 --> 00:17:13.283
(SPEAKS DOTHRAKI)

00:17:22.209 --> 00:17:23.752
Rakharo.

00:17:25.003 --> 00:17:27.798
You are my last hope, blood of my blood.

00:17:28.424 --> 00:17:31.385
I will not fail you, blood of my blood.

00:17:32.469 --> 00:17:34.304
You never have.

00:17:39.643 --> 00:17:42.771
This is bad time to start.

00:17:56.577 --> 00:17:58.495
(HORSE WHINNIES)

00:18:19.683 --> 00:18:21.518
(WIND HOWLING)

00:18:39.161 --> 00:18:41.121
Having a rough time of it?

00:18:41.205 --> 00:18:42.706
Nothing's killed me yet.

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:45.459
- GRENN: Your arse killed the sledge. - You offered me a ride.

00:18:45.542 --> 00:18:48.462
I just wanted you to shut up about your damn blisters.

00:19:02.768 --> 00:19:05.521
I was born in a place like this.

00:19:05.604 --> 00:19:08.524
Later, I fell on hard times.

00:19:10.317 --> 00:19:12.027
SAMWELL: Are those girls?

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:13.862
DOLOROUS EDD: Craster's daughters.

00:19:14.613 --> 00:19:17.574
I haven't seen a girl in six months.

00:19:17.991 --> 00:19:19.743
I'd keep on not seeing them if I were you.

00:19:20.744 --> 00:19:22.913
What, he don't like people messing with his daughters?

00:19:22.996 --> 00:19:25.582
He don't like people messing with his wives.

00:19:28.085 --> 00:19:31.421
He marries his daughters, and they give him more daughters.

00:19:31.505 --> 00:19:33.590
And on and on it goes.

00:19:34.216 --> 00:19:36.552
- That's foul. - It's beyond foul.

00:19:36.635 --> 00:19:40.472
All the other wildlings for a hundred leagues have disappeared.

00:19:40.556 --> 00:19:42.516
Craster's still here.

00:19:42.599 --> 00:19:45.018
He must be doing something right.

00:19:46.854 --> 00:19:48.522
What happens to the boys?

00:19:48.605 --> 00:19:49.731
Hmm?

00:19:49.815 --> 00:19:51.525
He marries his daughters.

00:19:52.276 --> 00:19:54.486
What does he do with his sons?

00:19:57.281 --> 00:20:01.076
He said he planned to stop here on his way to the Frostfangs.

00:20:01.159 --> 00:20:02.744
People make all sorts of plans.

00:20:02.828 --> 00:20:06.206
I haven't seen Benjen Stark in three years.

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:07.708
Haven't missed him.

00:20:07.791 --> 00:20:10.377
Always treated me like scum.

00:20:11.628 --> 00:20:14.464
Haven't had any good wine for a long time.

00:20:14.548 --> 00:20:17.384
You Southerners make good wine, I'll give you that.

00:20:17.467 --> 00:20:19.386
We're not Southerners.

00:20:19.469 --> 00:20:21.096
Who's this little girl?

00:20:22.723 --> 00:20:25.434
You're prettier than half my daughters.

00:20:25.517 --> 00:20:28.812
You got a nice wet twat between your legs?

00:20:28.896 --> 00:20:30.647
What's your name?

00:20:30.731 --> 00:20:32.649
- Jon Snow. - Snow, eh?

00:20:32.816 --> 00:20:35.652
Listen to me, bastard.

00:20:35.777 --> 00:20:39.698
All you lot from south of the Wall, you're Southerners.

00:20:39.781 --> 00:20:43.452
But now you're in the North, the real North.

00:20:43.744 --> 00:20:44.995
The lad meant no harm.

00:20:46.663 --> 00:20:50.083
I catch that pretty little bastard talking to my daughters...

00:20:50.167 --> 00:20:54.046
No one will talk to your daughters, you have my word.

00:20:54.129 --> 00:20:57.174
Now, sit down and shut your mouth.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:02.429
You bring any of that good wine with you?

00:21:02.512 --> 00:21:04.097
We did.

00:21:04.222 --> 00:21:06.808
We passed through six villages on the way here.

00:21:06.892 --> 00:21:08.769
All six were abandoned.

00:21:09.811 --> 00:21:11.730
Where have all the wildlings gone?

00:21:11.813 --> 00:21:15.192
I could tell you, but I'm thirsty.

00:21:15.651 --> 00:21:17.653
MORMONT: There's a barrel of Dornish wine on the sledge.

00:21:17.736 --> 00:21:20.322
- Bring it in here. - MAN: Yes, Commander.

00:21:20.405 --> 00:21:23.492
CRASTER: You want to know where they've all gone?

00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:27.579
North, to join up with Mance Rayder.

00:21:28.997 --> 00:21:30.707
Your old friend.

00:21:31.083 --> 00:21:33.335
He's no friend of mine.

00:21:33.418 --> 00:21:37.798
- He broke his vows, betrayed his brothers. - Aye.

00:21:37.881 --> 00:21:40.968
But once he was just a poor black crow.

00:21:41.051 --> 00:21:43.887
And now he's King-beyond-the-Wall.

00:21:43.971 --> 00:21:46.390
He's been calling himself that for years.

00:21:46.473 --> 00:21:50.060
What's he king of? A frozen lake somewhere?

00:21:51.561 --> 00:21:53.605
That's a good-looking ax.

00:21:53.689 --> 00:21:55.649
Fresh forged?

00:21:57.776 --> 00:21:59.236
Give it here.

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:02.531
You'll have another one made at Castle Black.

00:22:02.614 --> 00:22:04.574
Here.

00:22:05.993 --> 00:22:08.120
That's some lovely steel.

00:22:12.082 --> 00:22:15.002
You want to know what Mance Rayder is doing?

00:22:15.085 --> 00:22:16.420
Gathering an army.

00:22:17.295 --> 00:22:20.841
What I hear, he's already got more men than any of your Southern Kings.

00:22:20.924 --> 00:22:24.177
And where does he plan marching this army?

00:22:24.261 --> 00:22:27.222
When you're all the way north, there's only one direction to go.

00:22:29.599 --> 00:22:33.812
These are bad times to be living alone in the wild.

00:22:34.271 --> 00:22:36.314
The cold winds are rising.

00:22:37.607 --> 00:22:41.028
Let them come. My roots are sunk deep.

00:22:42.612 --> 00:22:44.573
Wife,

00:22:44.656 --> 00:22:48.618
tell the Lord Crow how content we are.

00:22:49.077 --> 00:22:51.038
This is our place.

00:22:51.121 --> 00:22:52.914
Our husband keeps us safe.

00:22:52.998 --> 00:22:56.001
Better to live free than die a slave.

00:22:58.545 --> 00:23:01.506
CRASTER: Don't it make you jealous, old man,

00:23:01.590 --> 00:23:06.887
to see me with all these young wives and you with no one to warm your bed?

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:09.014
We chose different paths.

00:23:09.097 --> 00:23:13.268
Aye, and you chose the path with no one but boys on it.

00:23:15.312 --> 00:23:18.273
You'll be wanting to sleep beneath my roof, I suppose,

00:23:18.356 --> 00:23:20.442
and eat me out of pigs.

00:23:20.525 --> 00:23:22.402
A roof would be welcome.

00:23:22.486 --> 00:23:23.904
It's been hard riding.

00:23:23.987 --> 00:23:27.199
We've brought our own food and good steel for you.

00:23:29.826 --> 00:23:32.537
Any man lays a hand on one of my wives,

00:23:33.413 --> 00:23:35.248
he loses the hand.

00:23:37.459 --> 00:23:41.213
And I see this one staring too long,

00:23:41.296 --> 00:23:44.299
I might just gouge his eyes out.

00:23:44.508 --> 00:23:47.719
Your roof, your rules.

00:23:59.231 --> 00:24:00.649
(GRUNTS)

00:24:00.732 --> 00:24:02.400
Who am I?

00:24:03.193 --> 00:24:06.613
- Who am I? - Lord Commander.

00:24:06.696 --> 00:24:09.783
- And who are you? - Jon Snow.

00:24:09.866 --> 00:24:11.243
Who are you?

00:24:12.702 --> 00:24:14.204
Your steward.

00:24:14.704 --> 00:24:16.706
You want to lead one day?

00:24:19.751 --> 00:24:21.962
Then learn how to follow.

00:24:35.851 --> 00:24:37.519
(MAN PANTING)

00:24:39.521 --> 00:24:43.233
MELISANDRE: Lord of Light, come to us in our darkness.

00:24:44.234 --> 00:24:47.362
We offer you these false gods.

00:24:48.280 --> 00:24:51.116
Take them and cast your light upon us,

00:24:52.909 --> 00:24:56.246
for the night is dark and full of terrors.

00:24:57.080 --> 00:25:00.250
MEN: For the night is dark and full of terrors.

00:25:02.627 --> 00:25:04.546
MELISANDRE: After the long summer,

00:25:04.629 --> 00:25:07.507
darkness will fall heavy on the world.

00:25:07.591 --> 00:25:10.177
The stars will bleed.

00:25:10.343 --> 00:25:12.846
We need to stop her.

00:25:12.929 --> 00:25:16.683
MELISANDRE: The cold breath of winter will freeze the seas...

00:25:16.766 --> 00:25:20.937
- Not now. - ...and the dead shall rise in the North.

00:25:22.647 --> 00:25:26.276
All you men were named in the light of the Seven!

00:25:26.359 --> 00:25:29.404
Is this how you treat the gods of your fathers?

00:25:29.487 --> 00:25:34.075
Are you so eager to spit on your ancestors?

00:25:42.751 --> 00:25:45.086
You smell of fear,

00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:49.132
fear and piss and old bones.

00:25:50.634 --> 00:25:52.219
Do you want to stop me?

00:25:56.848 --> 00:25:58.600
Stop me.

00:26:11.613 --> 00:26:13.281
In the ancient books, it's written

00:26:13.365 --> 00:26:17.077
that a warrior will draw a burning sword from the fire.

00:26:18.328 --> 00:26:21.414
And that sword shall be Lightbringer.

00:26:26.336 --> 00:26:29.798
Stannis Baratheon,

00:26:29.881 --> 00:26:32.384
Warrior of Light,

00:26:32.467 --> 00:26:34.219
your sword awaits you.

00:26:55.740 --> 00:26:57.492
(MEN CHEERING)

00:27:05.208 --> 00:27:07.961
MEN: Lord, cast your light upon us!

00:27:09.671 --> 00:27:12.841
MELISANDRE: For the night is dark and full of terrors.

00:27:15.969 --> 00:27:19.097
For the night is dark and full of terror.

00:27:46.416 --> 00:27:50.003
This woman will lead him into a war he cannot win.

00:27:50.086 --> 00:27:51.671
Stannis is our king.

00:27:51.755 --> 00:27:53.173
We follow where he leads,

00:27:53.256 --> 00:27:55.759
- even if we don't like the path. - King.

00:27:55.842 --> 00:27:59.929
Since that boar killed his brother, every lord wants a coronation.

00:28:00.013 --> 00:28:02.182
I don't serve the others. I serve Stannis.

00:28:02.265 --> 00:28:03.892
As do I,

00:28:03.975 --> 00:28:07.604
but loyal service means telling hard truths.

00:28:08.897 --> 00:28:11.691
He's surrounded by fools and fanatics,

00:28:12.984 --> 00:28:15.820
but he trusts you, Davos.

00:28:15.904 --> 00:28:18.490
If you tell him the truth...

00:28:20.283 --> 00:28:21.951
What's the truth?

00:28:34.923 --> 00:28:38.176
MATTHOS: "And I declare upon the honor of my house that my beloved brother Robert..."

00:28:38.259 --> 00:28:40.804
He wasn't my beloved brother.

00:28:40.970 --> 00:28:42.972
I didn't love him. He didn't love me.

00:28:43.056 --> 00:28:44.891
A harmless courtesy, Your Grace.

00:28:44.974 --> 00:28:46.017
A lie. Take it out.

00:28:49.229 --> 00:28:51.106
"That my brother Robert left no trueborn heirs,

00:28:51.773 --> 00:28:55.777
"the boy Joffrey, the boy Tommen, and the girl Myrcella being born of incest

00:28:55.860 --> 00:28:58.905
"between Cersei Lannister and her brother Jaime Lannister.

00:28:58.988 --> 00:29:01.741
- "By right of birth..." - Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer.

00:29:01.825 --> 00:29:03.159
Call him what he is.

00:29:05.328 --> 00:29:07.664
"And her brother Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer."

00:29:07.747 --> 00:29:11.042
"By right of birth and blood, I do this day lay claim..."

00:29:11.126 --> 00:29:14.003
STANNIS: Make it Ser Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer.

00:29:14.087 --> 00:29:16.131
Whatever else he is, the man's still a knight.

00:29:16.214 --> 00:29:18.550
"Ser Jaime Lannister, the Kingslayer.

00:29:18.633 --> 00:29:20.844
"By right of birth and blood,

00:29:20.927 --> 00:29:23.972
"I do this day lay claim to the Iron Throne of Westeros.

00:29:24.097 --> 00:29:26.683
"Let all true men declare their loyalty."

00:29:26.766 --> 00:29:29.060
When Eddard Stark learned the truth, he told only me.

00:29:29.144 --> 00:29:31.354
I'll not make the same mistake.

00:29:31.438 --> 00:29:33.440
Send copies of that letter to every corner of the realm,

00:29:33.523 --> 00:29:35.442
from the Arbor to the Wall.

00:29:35.525 --> 00:29:37.694
The time has come to choose.

00:29:38.486 --> 00:29:40.864
Let no man claim ignorance as an excuse.

00:29:40.947 --> 00:29:43.450
Your Grace, the Lannisters are the true enemy.

00:29:43.533 --> 00:29:45.618
If, for the time being, you could make peace with your brother...

00:29:45.702 --> 00:29:47.787
I'll not make peace with Renly while he calls himself king.

00:29:47.871 --> 00:29:49.664
Well, many have already declared for him,

00:29:49.747 --> 00:29:51.958
Mace Tyrell, Randyll Tarly.

00:29:52.041 --> 00:29:55.253
Stannis does not need to beg this lord or that lord for support.

00:29:55.336 --> 00:29:56.838
The Lord of Light stands behind him.

00:29:56.921 --> 00:30:00.175
And how many ships has the Lord of Light got in his fleet?

00:30:00.258 --> 00:30:02.719
- He has no need for ships. - DAVOS: I'm sure he doesn't,

00:30:02.802 --> 00:30:04.345
but we do if we're going to war.

00:30:04.888 --> 00:30:07.474
If not Renly, Your Grace, join forces with Robb Stark.

00:30:07.557 --> 00:30:09.642
Who would steal the northern half of my kingdom.

00:30:09.726 --> 00:30:13.146
I've always served thieves according to their deserts, as you well know, Ser Davos.

00:30:13.229 --> 00:30:16.274
Joffrey, Renly, Robb Stark, they're all thieves.

00:30:16.357 --> 00:30:18.776
They'll bend the knee or I'll destroy them.

00:30:19.611 --> 00:30:22.572
I owe you an apology, my king.

00:30:23.406 --> 00:30:25.366
My duty is to serve.

00:30:25.450 --> 00:30:29.579
You have chosen the new god over the old gods.

00:30:29.662 --> 00:30:33.041
May the Lord of Light watch over us all.

00:30:33.124 --> 00:30:35.460
Shall we drink together?

00:30:35.543 --> 00:30:37.003
Don't.

00:30:37.545 --> 00:30:42.091
A cup of wine to honor the one true god.

00:31:25.051 --> 00:31:26.052
(THUDS)

00:31:26.135 --> 00:31:27.136
(MEN MURMURING)

00:31:28.471 --> 00:31:31.641
The night is dark and full of terrors, old man,

00:31:31.724 --> 00:31:34.811
but the fire burns them all away.

00:31:40.066 --> 00:31:42.193
(CHATTER)

00:32:09.929 --> 00:32:11.848
King in the North.

00:32:14.601 --> 00:32:18.313
I keep expecting you to leave me in one castle or another for safekeeping,

00:32:18.396 --> 00:32:21.274
but you drag me along from camp to camp.

00:32:22.900 --> 00:32:25.111
Have you grown fond of me, Stark?

00:32:25.194 --> 00:32:26.988
Is that it?

00:32:27.071 --> 00:32:28.865
I've never seen you with a girl.

00:32:29.991 --> 00:32:32.452
If I left you with one of my bannermen,

00:32:32.535 --> 00:32:35.538
your father would know within a fortnight

00:32:35.622 --> 00:32:39.167
and my bannerman would receive a raven with a message,

00:32:39.250 --> 00:32:42.795
"Release my son and you'll be rich beyond your dreams.

00:32:42.879 --> 00:32:46.299
"Refuse and your house will be destroyed, root and stem."

00:32:46.382 --> 00:32:50.887
You don't trust the loyalty of the men following you into battle?

00:32:50.970 --> 00:32:53.014
Oh, I trust them with my life,

00:32:54.432 --> 00:32:55.558
just not with yours.

00:32:56.351 --> 00:32:58.144
Smart boy.

00:32:58.394 --> 00:33:00.146
What's wrong?

00:33:00.229 --> 00:33:01.814
Don't like being called "boy"?

00:33:03.024 --> 00:33:04.734
Insulted?

00:33:06.569 --> 00:33:08.154
(GREY WIND SNARLING)

00:33:12.033 --> 00:33:14.744
ROBB: You insult yourself, Kingslayer.

00:33:16.746 --> 00:33:18.998
- You've been defeated by a boy. - (HEAVY BREATHING)

00:33:20.083 --> 00:33:22.210
You're held captive by a boy.

00:33:25.129 --> 00:33:26.923
Perhaps you'll be killed by a boy.

00:33:33.971 --> 00:33:37.558
Stannis Baratheon sent ravens to all the high lords of Westeros.

00:33:39.143 --> 00:33:42.689
King Joffrey Baratheon is neither a true king

00:33:42.772 --> 00:33:45.400
nor a true Baratheon.

00:33:45.983 --> 00:33:47.694
He's your bastard son.

00:33:47.777 --> 00:33:50.113
If that's true, Stannis is the rightful king.

00:33:50.196 --> 00:33:52.240
How convenient for him.

00:33:52.949 --> 00:33:56.577
My father learned the truth.

00:33:56.661 --> 00:33:58.287
That's why you had him executed.

00:33:58.371 --> 00:34:00.623
I was your prisoner when Ned Stark lost his head.

00:34:00.707 --> 00:34:04.377
Your son killed him so the world wouldn't learn who fathered him.

00:34:04.460 --> 00:34:05.712
And you,

00:34:06.921 --> 00:34:10.091
you pushed my brother from a window because he saw you with the queen.

00:34:15.263 --> 00:34:17.306
You have proof?

00:34:18.641 --> 00:34:21.060
Or do you want to trade gossip like a couple of fishwives?

00:34:21.144 --> 00:34:25.022
I'm sending one of your cousins down to King's Landing with my peace terms.

00:34:25.106 --> 00:34:27.525
You think my father's going to negotiate with you?

00:34:28.443 --> 00:34:30.445
You don't know him very well.

00:34:30.528 --> 00:34:34.115
No, but he's starting to know me.

00:34:35.158 --> 00:34:38.453
Three victories don't make you a conqueror.

00:34:39.829 --> 00:34:41.497
It's better than three defeats.

00:34:50.381 --> 00:34:52.008
(SNARLING)

00:35:11.110 --> 00:35:12.820
SHAE: This city stinks.

00:35:16.073 --> 00:35:17.658
Like dead bodies.

00:35:17.742 --> 00:35:19.827
TYRION: A bit corpsey, yes.

00:35:20.703 --> 00:35:22.371
And shit.

00:35:22.455 --> 00:35:24.040
I thought you wanted to come here.

00:35:27.585 --> 00:35:29.086
I love it.

00:35:30.046 --> 00:35:33.049
You love the smell of dead bodies and shit?

00:35:33.800 --> 00:35:36.677
And cum and garlic and rum.

00:35:36.761 --> 00:35:39.263
You can smell cum from the balcony?

00:35:40.056 --> 00:35:43.309
I love the stink. I love the noise.

00:35:43.392 --> 00:35:45.394
Cities make me want to fuck.

00:35:46.395 --> 00:35:48.564
And so did the country.

00:35:50.274 --> 00:35:51.734
(SIGHS)

00:35:51.818 --> 00:35:53.319
This is where I belong.

00:35:53.402 --> 00:35:56.197
Yes, well, you need to be careful.

00:35:56.280 --> 00:35:57.824
No one can know you're here.

00:35:57.907 --> 00:35:59.492
No one will know.

00:35:59.575 --> 00:36:01.285
You can't trust anyone in King's Landing.

00:36:01.369 --> 00:36:04.330
They're all liars, good liars, bad liars,

00:36:04.413 --> 00:36:06.833
one or two great liars.

00:36:06.916 --> 00:36:08.793
What about you?

00:36:08.876 --> 00:36:11.629
Me? I'm not from here. I'm a slave to the truth.

00:36:13.297 --> 00:36:14.382
(LAUGHS) Truth?

00:36:16.342 --> 00:36:19.345
You are the biggest little liar I have ever met.

00:36:19.428 --> 00:36:21.389
Why do you think I am so little?

00:36:21.472 --> 00:36:25.768
I'm being crushed beneath the weight of all that truth.

00:36:30.231 --> 00:36:32.984
Ned Stark actually slept on this.

00:36:33.067 --> 00:36:36.696
As if the poor man didn't suffer enough.

00:36:38.614 --> 00:36:42.118
One of the many changes we'll have to make around here.

00:36:53.296 --> 00:36:55.214
Lord Baelish.

00:36:55.298 --> 00:36:56.549
Your Grace.

00:36:56.632 --> 00:36:59.093
I wonder if I might ask you for a favor.

00:36:59.176 --> 00:37:00.720
Of course, Your Grace.

00:37:00.803 --> 00:37:02.722
Ned Stark's youngest daughter Arya,

00:37:02.805 --> 00:37:04.974
we can't seem to locate her.

00:37:05.641 --> 00:37:09.604
If she's escaped the capital, Winterfell seems the logical destination.

00:37:09.687 --> 00:37:12.106
And yet my friends in the North report no sign of her.

00:37:12.189 --> 00:37:14.066
Curious.

00:37:14.150 --> 00:37:16.235
If we choose to negotiate with the Starks,

00:37:16.319 --> 00:37:18.321
the girl has some value. Whoever finds her...

00:37:18.404 --> 00:37:20.656
Well, you know what they say about Lannisters and debts.

00:37:20.740 --> 00:37:23.117
Well, you could ask Varys where she is.

00:37:24.201 --> 00:37:25.453
He'll have an answer for you.

00:37:25.536 --> 00:37:26.954
Whether you believe it...

00:37:27.038 --> 00:37:31.042
Myself, I have always had a hard time trusting eunuchs.

00:37:31.125 --> 00:37:33.586
Who knows what they want?

00:37:33.669 --> 00:37:35.588
A mockingbird.

00:37:36.881 --> 00:37:39.675
- You created your own sigil, didn't you? - Yes.

00:37:40.468 --> 00:37:44.430
Appropriate, for a self-made man with so many songs to sing.

00:37:44.513 --> 00:37:46.098
I'm glad you like it.

00:37:46.182 --> 00:37:49.644
Some people are fortunate enough to be born into the right family.

00:37:49.727 --> 00:37:52.188
Others have to find their own way.

00:37:53.731 --> 00:37:55.775
I heard a song once

00:37:55.858 --> 00:37:58.444
about a boy of modest means

00:37:58.527 --> 00:38:01.030
who found his way into the home of a very prominent family.

00:38:02.365 --> 00:38:03.991
He loved the eldest daughter.

00:38:04.075 --> 00:38:06.410
Sadly, she had eyes for another.

00:38:07.828 --> 00:38:11.749
When boys and girls live in the same home, awkward situations can arise.

00:38:12.625 --> 00:38:17.129
Sometimes, I've heard, even brothers and sisters develop certain affections.

00:38:17.797 --> 00:38:20.216
And when those affections become common knowledge,

00:38:20.299 --> 00:38:24.136
well, that is an awkward situation indeed,

00:38:24.220 --> 00:38:26.347
especially in a prominent family.

00:38:26.430 --> 00:38:28.724
But prominent families often forget a simple truth,

00:38:29.725 --> 00:38:31.185
I've found.

00:38:32.269 --> 00:38:34.271
And which truth is that?

00:38:34.355 --> 00:38:36.691
Knowledge is power.

00:38:40.236 --> 00:38:42.488
Seize him.

00:38:44.448 --> 00:38:46.242
Cut his throat.

00:38:46.909 --> 00:38:49.078
Stop. Wait.

00:38:50.079 --> 00:38:52.248
I've changed my mind. Let him go.

00:38:55.292 --> 00:38:56.919
Step back three paces.

00:38:58.504 --> 00:39:00.131
Turn around.

00:39:00.923 --> 00:39:02.341
Close your eyes.

00:39:06.721 --> 00:39:08.264
Power is power.

00:39:10.933 --> 00:39:14.687
Do see if you can take some time away from your coins and your whores

00:39:14.770 --> 00:39:16.605
to locate the Stark girl for me.

00:39:16.689 --> 00:39:19.358
I would very much appreciate it.

00:39:30.077 --> 00:39:32.121
ROBB: You're Ser Alton Lannister?

00:39:32.788 --> 00:39:34.790
I am, Your Grace.

00:39:34.874 --> 00:39:38.252
ROBB: I offer your cousins peace if they meet my terms.

00:39:38.377 --> 00:39:42.631
First, your family must release my sisters.

00:39:43.299 --> 00:39:46.260
Second, my father's bones must be returned to us

00:39:46.343 --> 00:39:51.057
so he may rest beside his brother and sister in the crypts beneath Winterfell.

00:39:51.140 --> 00:39:55.144
And the remains of all those who died in his service must also be returned.

00:39:55.644 --> 00:39:58.105
Their families can honor them with proper funerals.

00:39:58.189 --> 00:40:00.983
- An honorable request, Your Grace. - Third...

00:40:02.818 --> 00:40:07.323
Joffrey and the Queen Regent must renounce all claim to dominion of the North.

00:40:07.990 --> 00:40:12.661
From this time till the end of time, we are a free and independent kingdom.

00:40:12.745 --> 00:40:14.747
The King in the North.

00:40:14.830 --> 00:40:17.249
- King in the North. - King in the North.

00:40:17.333 --> 00:40:21.045
Neither Joffrey nor any of his men shall set foot in our lands again.

00:40:21.128 --> 00:40:23.130
If he disregards this command,

00:40:23.214 --> 00:40:26.092
he shall suffer the same fate as my father,

00:40:26.675 --> 00:40:30.930
only I don't need a servant to do my beheading for me.

00:40:31.013 --> 00:40:34.391
These are... Your Grace, these are...

00:40:34.475 --> 00:40:36.977
These are my terms.

00:40:37.061 --> 00:40:40.147
If the Queen Regent and her son meet them, I'll give them peace.

00:40:40.231 --> 00:40:41.524
If not,

00:40:43.317 --> 00:40:45.778
I will litter the South with Lannister dead.

00:40:45.861 --> 00:40:48.572
King Joffrey is a Baratheon, Your Grace.

00:40:48.656 --> 00:40:50.199
Oh, is he?

00:40:51.659 --> 00:40:54.161
You'll ride at daybreak, Ser Alton.

00:40:55.037 --> 00:40:57.456
That will be all for tonight.

00:41:12.429 --> 00:41:14.431
A word, Your Grace?

00:41:16.350 --> 00:41:18.978
You don't have to call me "Your Grace" when no one's around.

00:41:19.061 --> 00:41:21.689
It's not so bad once you get used to it.

00:41:21.814 --> 00:41:23.732
I'm glad someone's gotten used to it.

00:41:24.733 --> 00:41:26.902
The Lannisters are going to reject your terms, you know?

00:41:26.986 --> 00:41:28.821
Of course they are.

00:41:28.904 --> 00:41:31.198
We can fight them in the fields as long as you like,

00:41:31.282 --> 00:41:34.577
but we won't beat them until you take King's Landing.

00:41:36.412 --> 00:41:39.623
And we can't take King's Landing without ships.

00:41:39.707 --> 00:41:42.168
My father has ships and men who know how to sail them.

00:41:42.251 --> 00:41:44.003
Men who fought my father.
